\f0\fs28\b Yamaha YAS-209 Sound Bar (YXC)\b0\fs20\par
\par
IP driver for the Yamaha YAS-209 sound bar using the Yamaha Extended Control (YXC) HTTP API on port 80. Presents to Control4 as a Receiver (power, volume, mute, input selection) plus extra Actions for sound modes and transport.\par
\par
\b Requirements\b0\par
\bullet  YAS-209 on the same network as the controller, reachable by IP.\par
\bullet  A DHCP reservation for the sound bar (strongly recommended).\par
\par
\b Setup\b0\par
1. Add the driver to the project and place it in the sound bar's room.\par
2. Set the \b IP Address\b0  property to the sound bar's IP (or assign the Network connection). \par
3. In Connections, bind the AUDIO/VIDEO OUTPUT end-point to the room, and connect any sources (cable box, Apple TV, etc.) to the HDMI In / Optical / TV inputs as wired.\par
4. Run Actions \endash  Query Features to log the sound bar's exact input and sound-program IDs. If they differ from the defaults, update the INPUT_MAP table in driver.lua.\par
\par
\b Properties\b0\par
\bullet  IP Address \endash  sound bar address (authoritative if set).\par
\bullet  Poll Interval Seconds \endash  how often state is refreshed (default 3).\par
\bullet  Use Push Events \endash  EXPERIMENTAL UDP status push; leave Off unless validated.\par
\bullet  Volume Ramp Step \endash  step size for volume up/down.\par
\bullet  Sound Program \endash  selecting a value sends it to the sound bar.\par
\par
\b Notes\b0\par
This driver controls the sound bar over its documented network API; it does not require MusicCast multiroom. Streaming sources (Spotify, Alexa) are driven by their own apps; this driver exposes transport (play/pause/next/previous) as Actions.\par
\par
Author: David Woychek (david@propertyrenewal.llc). Not affiliated with or endorsed by Yamaha.\par
